1. Design DNA & Visual Language (Railway.com Style)
Theme: Ultra-dark mode (#0a0a0a) with a subtle "inner glow" on cards (border-white/10).
Typography: Use a high-contrast sans-serif (Geist/Inter). Headers should be tracking-tighter, metadata tracking-widest.
Background: Use a 1px grid pattern (opacity 5%) and very subtle radial gradients (blue/indigo at 3% opacity) to provide depth without "AI Slop" gradients.
Glassmorphism: Apply backdrop-blur-xl and bg-neutral-900/40 to all floating elements.
2. Component Logic: The Multi-Agent Orchestrator
Orchestration Flow:
Thinking State: Use GSAP to animate a "Logic Stream" showing the routing between 5 agents (Audit, Cash, Mail, Compliance, Ops).
The Narrative: The main chat displays the AI's synthesized narrative.
Evidence Traces: Every response MUST include a "Source Attribution" row—a horizontal list of interactive chips (e.g., [Database: SQL_ERP], [Mail: Legal_Inbox]).
The Evidence Canvas: - Clicking a Source Chip triggers a Side-Canvas (60% width) or Compact Modal.
Crucial: The Canvas allows raw data validation (Tables, Doc viewers, Charts) without navigating away from the chat.
Use GSAP Expo.easeOut for the Canvas entrance for a premium, snappy feel.
3. Motion & Interaction (GSAP Specs)
Message Stagger: New messages must stagger in using gsap.from(el, { y: 20, opacity: 0, duration: 0.6, ease: "power4.out" }).
Magnetic Buttons: Apply subtle magnetic hover effects to primary action buttons.
Status Indicators: Use GSAP to animate "pulse" and "sync" states for the background agents during the orchestration phase.
4. Technical Constraints
Library Stack: Tailwind CSS, GSAP (for all complex motion), Lucide React (icons), and Shadcn UI (base components).
Mobile UX: The Evidence Canvas should transform into a Bottom Sheet on mobile devices.
Responsiveness: All layouts must be fluid; avoid fixed pixel widths for containers.